<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pshavi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pshavi is a historic mountain region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, in the valley of the Pshavi Aragvi river. Its people, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pshavs">Pshavs</a>, lived in clan communities with their own shrines and customs, and with the neighbouring highlanders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tusheti">Tusheti</a> and Khevsureti they supplied warriors to the kings of Kakheti. The poet Vazha-Pshavela took his pen name from the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pshavi.jpg" alt="Pshavi" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giorgi Balakhadze · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historical_Pshavi_in_modern_international_borders_of_Georgia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
